   "text": {
    "L1": "India has many languages, foods, styles of dress and festivals.",
    "L2": "Unity does not mean everyone must become the same.",
    "L3": "Different ways of living can share common values and belonging.",
    "L4": "Look at harvest festivals around mid-January.",
    "L5": "Pongal, Bihu and Lohri have different names and customs.",
    "L6": "Their shared thread is a winter harvest and thanks for crops.",
    "L7": "The Ramayana is one story retold in many languages and forms.",
    "L8": "That is unity in diversity: many forms, held together."
   },
